# run-7's working copies of ONE checkpoint. Four of them, ~105 MB each, all reconstructible:
# the TARBALL is the digest-verified artifact (bound by the reorg manifest), calibrate.sh
# extracts from it into .calib-work, and build_artifact.sh keeps a fetched copy plus a nested one.
#
# Ignored as DIRECTORIES, deliberately. The root .gitignore's small-evidence allowlist
# (!runs/**/*.json, *.md, *.log, *.txt) re-includes the metadata INSIDE a checkpoint directory,
# so without this the repo would start tracking checkpoints/*/lora/README.md,
# checkpoints/*.json, checkpoints/history.json and so on. That is exactly
# the failure the root file's `runs/**/ckpt-*/` rule records -- and that rule misses these,
# because these directories are named `checkpoints/`, not `ckpt-*/`.
out/fetched/
out/checkpoints/
out/.artifact-check/
out/.artifact-check.prev.*/
fetched/

# out/calibrated/ is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the fitted config, 774 bytes, and the
# result of the run's calibration. run-6 tracks the equivalent file.
